==Trivia==
*Her hairstyle could be a reference to the famous Tim Burton movie, ''[[wikipedia:Mars Attacks!|Mars Attacks!]]''.
*The chihuahua in her English description may be [[King Wahwah]]'s kid brother, [[Everlord Wanwan]].
*Her Japanese name (プドール婦人 ''Pudōru Fujin'', "Lady Pudoll") may make a pun on プードル ''pūdoru'' (poodle) and ドール ''dōru'' (doll, a slang term for a good-looking woman).
*Her Japanese description mentioned King Wahwah by name 2 years before he was introduced.
*According to their Japanese descriptions, Mistress Celeboodle and King Wahwah are a [[wikipedia:Manzai|''manzai'']] comedy duo with Mistress Celeboodle as the ''tsukkomi'' (the short-tempered "straight man" who takes things seriously) and King Wahwah as the ''boke'' (the airheaded "funny man" who gets everything wrong).
**In [[Heaven-Defying Fruit]], Mistress Celeboodle and King Wahwah appear together alongside another comedian, [[Oldstrich]].

